  data: {
    LLM: 'The dealer deals all 51 cards one by one; some players may have one more card. Everyone discards any pairs (and from triplets or quartets, discard two or two pairs). The dealer offers their hand face down to the player on their left, who draws one card without looking. If it makes a pair they discard the pair. The player who drew then offers their hand to the next player left; play continues clockwise. Players drop out when their hand is empty. The player left holding the single Queen (the Old Maid) loses.',
    Player: 'The dealer deals all 51 cards one by one; some players may have one more card. Everyone discards any pairs (and from triplets or quartets, discard two or two pairs). The dealer offers their hand face down to the player on their left, who draws one card without looking. If it makes a pair they discard the pair. The player who drew then offers their hand to the next player left; play continues clockwise. Players drop out when their hand is empty. The player left holding the single Queen (the Old Maid) loses.',
    objective: 'Pair up and discard all your cards; the player left holding the single remaining Queen (the Old Maid) at the end loses.',
    gameplay: 'The dealer deals all 51 cards one by one; some players may have one more card. Everyone discards any pairs (and from triplets or quartets, discard two or two pairs). The dealer offers their hand face down to the player on their left, who draws one card without looking. If it makes a pair they discard the pair. The player who drew then offers their hand to the next player left; play continues clockwise. Players drop out when their hand is empty. The player left holding the single Queen (the Old Maid) loses.',
    keyRules: [
      'Pairs are two cards of equal rank (e.g. two sevens or two kings).',
      'The player who just drew a card offers their hand to the next player to their left.',
      'If you empty your hand you are safe and take no further part; turn passes to the next player.',
      'The holder of the single remaining Queen (Old Maid) at the end loses.',
    ],
